":4,"numoutlets":1},{"id":"obj-16","maxclass":"newobj","text":"t b clear","rect":[407,285,104,23],"patchingRect":[407,285,104,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":2},{"id":"obj-26","maxclass":"comment","text":"The live.miditool.out object is responsible for updating the contents of a MIDI clip. As long as you provide a valid dictionary to the inlet, it will work.\n\nA valid dictionary contains a \"notes\" key, and an array of note dictionaries each containing at least a \"pitch\", \"start_time\" and \"duration\" key. You can of course alter other properties of the note such as:\n\n- velocity\n- mute\n- probability\n- velocity_deviation\n- release_velocity\n\nA basic generator is show to the right.","rect":[32,197,308,239],"patchingRect":[32,197,308,239],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":16},{"id":"obj-11","maxclass":"newobj","text":"live.miditool.out","rect":[433,684,98,23],"patchingRect":[433,684,98,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0},{"id":"obj-5","maxclass":"button","text":"","rect":[407,197,24,24],"patchingRect":[407,197,24,24],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":1,"parameterEnable":0},{"id":"obj-1","maxclass":"newobj","text":"live.miditool.in","rect":[407,240,90,23],"patchingRect":[407,240,90,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":3},{"id":"obj-24","maxclass":"comment","text":"live.miditool.out only functions when used inside of Max for Live Generator or Transformation. You will need to copy the Max patch code into a Transformation or Generator device.","rect":[10,139,556,33],"patchingRect":[10,139,556,33],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial Bold","fontsize":12,"linecount":2},{"id":"obj-25","maxclass":"textbutton","text":"1","rect":[735,199,20,20],"patchingRect":[735,199,20,20],"ignoreclick":1,"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":3,"fontname":"Arial Bold","textcolor":[0.34902,0.34902,0.34902,1],"bgcolor":[0.9,0.65,0.05,1],"parameterEnable":0},{"id":"obj-6","maxclass":"comment","text":"bang causes live.miditool.in to start a generator","rect":[43